<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/infographic-ai-integration-map.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wght@600;700&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&display=swap">
<div class="n3l-ai-integration-map">
  <figure class="fig">
    <header class="mast">
      <span class="eyebrow brand-eyebrow">NEXT3LABS &mdash; AI integration, Singapore</span>
      <div class="title">The API call is 10%. <span class="hi">The rest is the project.</span></div>
      <p class="sub">Data access, boundaries and accountability are the real work behind an AI integration that belongs in your business.</p>
      <div class="mast-rule"></div>
    </header>

    <div class="split">
      <div class="half half--quick">
        <span class="eyebrow half-label">What takes an afternoon</span>
        <p class="half-line">Wiring a model into your <b>stack.</b></p>
      </div>
      <div class="half half--project">
        <span class="eyebrow half-label">What takes the project</span>
        <p class="half-line">An <b class="stop-em">access map, boundaries and ownership.</b></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="steps-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">The integration map &mdash; five decisions before launch</span>
      <span class="legend">Make each decision explicit</span>
    </div>

    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="step">
        <span class="idx num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <div class="body">
          <h3>Map the systems, not the use case</h3>
          <p>Sort what it needs to read vs write before scoping the feature.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="out">Access map (reads vs writes)</span>
      </li>
      <li class="step">
        <span class="idx num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <div class="body">
          <h3>Decide the model / system-of-record boundary</h3>
          <p>The model reads live from the system of truth, never caches its own copy.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="out">Live reads, no cached copies</span>
      </li>
      <li class="step step--gate">
        <span class="idx num" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
        <div class="body">
          <h3>Put a human-legible permission boundary on it</h3>
          <p>Write down which actions are autonomous and which need a person to confirm.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="out out--gate">Written action list (autonomous vs confirm-required)</span>
      </li>
      <li class="step">
        <span class="idx num" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
        <div class="body">
          <h3>Instrument every call before you trust it</h3>
          <p>Log every call and response so a failure is diagnosable in minutes.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="out">Full call/response log</span>
      </li>
      <li class="step step--last">
        <span class="idx num" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
        <div class="body">
          <h3>Assign a named owner before launch</h3>
          <p>Someone accountable for reading logs and deciding on scope changes.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="out out--done">Accountable owner, day one</span>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <section class="fails">
      <span class="eyebrow fails-label">Scope creep, not model error</span>
      <ul class="fail-list">
        <li class="fail-item"><span class="x" aria-hidden="true">&times;</span><b>Unscoped write access</b></li>
        <li class="fail-item"><span class="x" aria-hidden="true">&times;</span><b>Cached data that drifts</b></li>
        <li class="fail-item"><span class="x" aria-hidden="true">&times;</span><b>No log when something fails</b></li>
        <li class="fail-item"><span class="x" aria-hidden="true">&times;</span><b>No owner when it does</b></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <figcaption class="foot">
      <span class="mark-word">NEXT3LABS</span>
      <span>Reads before it writes &middot; next3labs.com</span>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
</div>
